<title>USA: Pennsylvania Housing repriced, yields raised.</title>
<headline>Pennsylvania Housing repriced, yields raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber Inc. said Tuesday it repriced and restructured Pennsylvania Housing Finance Agency's $75 million bond deal, raising yields in several maturities while leaving the top yield unchanged at 5.80 percent in 2029.</p>
<p>PENNSYLVANIA HOUSING FINANCE AGENCY</p>
<p>RE: $75,000,000*</p>
<p>SINGLE FAMILY MORTGAGE REVENUE BONDS, SER. 1997-59</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>NOTE REPRICING AND RESTRUCTURING.</p>
<p>WE WILL CONTINUE TO TAKE ORDERS ON THE 1999, 2000, 2002 THRU 2004 AND 2006</p>
<p>UNTIL 3:30PM E.D.S.T TODAY.</p>
